Implemented Vercel Web Analytics for the Spice Route project.

## Summary
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics following the latest official documentation from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- Installed `@vercel/analytics` version 2.0.1
- Updated package.json and package-lock.json accordingly

### 2. Analytics Integration
- Modified: `/src/app/layout.tsx`
  - Added import: `import { Analytics } from '@vercel/analytics/next'`
  - Added `<Analytics />` component at the end of the `<body>` tag
  - Placement ensures analytics tracking is active across all pages

## Implementation Details

### Framework-Specific Configuration
This project uses **Next.js 14.1.0 with App Router**, so I followed the Next.js App Router instructions from the official Vercel documentation:

1. Imported the Analytics component from `@vercel/analytics/next`
2. Placed the component in the root layout file (`app/layout.tsx`)
3. Added it at the end of the `<body>` tag to ensure proper tracking initialization

### Code Structure Preserved
- Maintained existing component hierarchy
- Preserved all existing imports and dependencies
- Kept the established code style and formatting
- Analytics component added after existing components (ReactQueryProvider, Toaster, CookieConsentBanner)

## Verification

✅ TypeScript type checking passed (`npm run type-check`)
✅ Package successfully installed
✅ Analytics component properly imported and integrated
✅ No TypeScript errors introduced
✅ Existing code structure preserved

## Next Steps for Deployment

To complete the Vercel Analytics setup:
1. Deploy the application to Vercel
2. Enable Analytics in the Vercel project dashboard (Analytics tab → Enable button)
3. Verify tracking by checking browser Network tab for `/_vercel/insights/*` requests after deployment
4. Monitor analytics data in the Vercel dashboard

## Notes
- The build command failed due to missing Supabase environment variables, which is expected in this sandbox environment and unrelated to the Analytics integration
- All Analytics-related code changes are correct and ready for deployment
- The Analytics component will automatically track page views and web vitals once deployed to Vercel
